IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`

-- Land Tax Act 1936 (SA) -- the owner of land: who is liable, the residential land exemption, the taxable value, the scale,
-- aggregation, more than one owner, and the owner's duties to notify and to pay. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the
-- Act's own actors and terms ("the owner", "a natural person", "the taxpayer", "the Commissioner"). The individual's
-- questions are in lta-seat.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, through the Open Australian Legal Corpus
-- (CC BY 4.0; see lta-common.l4 and SOURCE-LICENSE.md). The deposited text is the Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at
-- 2023-07-01 (version_id south_australian_legislation:2023-07-01/1936.2318.un, scraped 2024-09-13), at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/land-tax-act-1936.txt. It is NOT the official text. The Current Titles list of
-- 22 September 2026 lists the Act at 4.12.2025, so the text is out of date. Every year's thresholds, and any change to
-- the rates after 1 July 2023, are INPUTS.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 2 ("owner", "residential land exemption", "site value", s 2(1c) capacities); s 4(1)(n), (2), (3)
-- (imposition; liability arises on 1 July, calculated at midnight on 30 June before); s 5(1), (2), (6)-(9), (10)(a),
-- (ab), (ac), (ad), (b), (ba), (bb), (e), (f), (h), (10a), (10b), (10c), (11a), (12), (12a), (13) (the residential land
-- exemption and its neighbours; s 5(7) as a regulative rule); s 5AA (a minor interest disregarded); s 5A (waiver or
-- refund for residential land); s 6 (minimum tax); s 7 (taxable value: the site value, an INPUT); s 8A(1), (2), (3a),
-- (7), (8) (thresholds: INPUTS, with the amounts the text states; rounding); Schedule 1 Part 1 and Part 2 clauses 2 and 3
-- (the scales, as tables); s 8B (aggregation, apportionment); s 9(1), (2), (4), (6), (8) (deduction an INPUT), (9);
-- ss 14-17 (liability; change of ownership; joint and several; distribution of burden); s 19(1) (pay within 30 days, a
-- regulative rule, run beside TAA s 91), s 19(2), (3).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: trusts (ss 11-13F, Schedule 1 Part 3, the s 13D trustee notices) except the special disability trust
-- (s 5(10)(h), (12a)); related corporations (ss 13G-13J); build-to-rent (s 7A); community and strata plans (s 10);
-- primary production and the other non-residential exemptions in s 4(1) and s 5(10)(c), (ca), (cb), (d), (g);
-- enforcement (ss 18, 20-24); service (s 25); regulations (s 26); the s 8A(2a), (3), (3b) indexation formulas and the
-- s 9(8) deduction formula, which are MISSING from the deposited text (see ../../registers/source-bundle/
-- land-tax-act-1936.formulas.md); the Land Tax Regulations (not deposited), including any further s 5(11) criteria and
-- the s 5A(1)(c)(v) and (d)(v) criteria, which are asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Land Tax Act 1936 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `ss 2, 4, 9(2), 14 -- who is the owner, and when the tax is fixed`

-- s 2(1) "owner -- (a) in relation to land alienated from the Crown by grant in fee simple means any person (other than a
-- mortgagee of the land) -- (i) who holds; or (ii) who is entitled to; or (iii) who is entitled to purchase or acquire, a
-- legal or equitable estate of fee simple in the land or any other estate or interest (other than an estate or interest
-- of leasehold) in the land conferring a right to possession of the land; and (b) in relation to land of the Crown subject
-- to any agreement for sale, or right of purchase, means the person entitled to the benefit of that agreement or right of
-- purchase; and (c) ... perpetual lease, means the holder of that lease; and (d) ... shack site lease, means the holder of
-- that lease; and (e) in relation to land in a defined shack-site area, means the occupier of the land".
-- s 2(1c): "the various capacities in which a person may be the owner of land are as follows: (a) as legal owner; (b) as
-- equitable owner; (c) as prospective owner (ie a person who has entered into a contract to purchase or acquire an estate
-- or interest in the land); (d) as lessee under a perpetual lease or a shack-site lease; (e) if the land is in a defined
-- shack-site area -- as occupier."
DECLARE `Capacity` IS ONE OF
    `legal owner`
    `equitable owner`
    `prospective owner, under a contract to purchase or acquire the land`
    `lessee under a perpetual lease or a shack site lease`
    `occupier of land in a defined shack-site area`
    `mortgagee only`
    `tenant under an ordinary lease only`
    `no estate or interest in the land`

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A `Capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an owner of the land` IF
    CONSIDER `the capacity`
    WHEN `mortgagee only` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `tenant under an ordinary lease only` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no estate or interest in the land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(2): "The taxes are imposed and payable in respect of every financial year and liability to the taxes arises at the
-- commencement of every financial year." (3): they "will, subject to this Act, be calculated as at midnight on 30 June
-- immediately preceding that financial year on the basis of circumstances then existing." s 7(2) takes the site value
-- "as at midnight on 30 June immediately preceding the commencement of that financial year".
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day at whose midnight the land tax is calculated` MEANS
    `the last day of the financial year` (`the financial year` MINUS 1)

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day liability for the land tax arises` MEANS `the first day of the financial year` `the financial year`

-- s 14(1): "Subject to this Act, an owner of land is liable for tax in respect of that land." (2): the person named as
-- owner in the valuation roll "will be presumed, in the absence of proof to the contrary, to be the owner".
-- s 9(1): s 9 "applies where 2 or more persons are the owners of the same land (whether in the same or in different
-- capacities)". (2): "If 2 or more persons are owners of the same land but not all in the same capacity, the Commissioner
-- may treat all who are owners of the land in a particular capacity (to be determined by the Commissioner) as -- (a) the
-- sole owner or owners of the land; and (b) the sole taxpayer or taxpayers for the land." The choice is the
-- Commissioner's: the answer is conditional on it.
DECLARE `Liability answer` IS ONE OF
    `liable for the land tax on the land`
    `liable, unless the Commissioner treats the owners in another capacity as the sole owners (s 9(2))`
    `not liable: not an owner of the land at midnight on 30 June before the year`

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A `Capacity`
      `another person owned the land in a different capacity at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`the person's liability for the land tax on the land` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the person is an owner of the land` `the capacity`))
    THEN `not liable: not an owner of the land at midnight on 30 June before the year`
    ELSE IF `another person owned the land in a different capacity at the same time`
         THEN `liable, unless the Commissioner treats the owners in another capacity as the sole owners (s 9(2))`
         ELSE `liable for the land tax on the land`

§§ `ss 15-17 -- change of ownership; joint and several liability; sharing the burden`

-- s 15(1): "no land and no person assessed for tax is relieved of a charge or liability for tax in respect of a particular
-- financial year by reason of a change in the ownership of the land, or any other event, occurring after the commencement
-- of the financial year."
`a change of ownership during the year relieves the liability for that year` MEANS FALSE

-- s 16: "Where there are two or more taxpayers in respect of the same land, they are jointly and severally liable to pay
-- tax in respect of that land."
GIVEN `the number of taxpayers for the land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each taxpayer can be made to pay all the tax on the land` IF
    `the number of taxpayers for the land` AT LEAST 2

-- s 17(1): "The burden of the tax will be distributed between the taxpayers in the relative proportions of the value of
-- their interests in the land taxed." (2): "A taxpayer who has paid tax in respect of land is entitled to recover from
-- every other taxpayer in respect of the same land a proper proportion of the amount paid."
GIVEN `the tax paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the payer's share of the value of the interests in the land, percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable from the other taxpayers` MEANS
    `the tax paid` TIMES (100 MINUS `the payer's share of the value of the interests in the land, percent`) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 5(10) and (12) -- the residential land exemption`

-- s 2(1): "residential land exemption means an exemption under section 5(10)(a), (ab), (ac), (ad), (b), (ba) or (bb)".
-- s 5(1): land is wholly exempt "if -- (a) proper grounds for the exemption exist; and (b) such an exemption has been
-- granted, and remains in force". (2): the same for a partial exemption. (3): an owner "may apply"; (5): the Commissioner
-- may exempt "whether or not an application for exemption has been made". This module answers whether PROPER GROUNDS
-- exist; whether the exemption has been granted is a fact.
DECLARE `Exemption paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 5(10)(a)`
    `s 5(10)(ab)`
    `s 5(10)(ac)`
    `s 5(10)(ad)`
    `s 5(10)(b)`
    `s 5(10)(ba)`
    `s 5(10)(bb)`
    `s 5(10)(e)`
    `s 5(10)(f)`
    `s 5(10)(h)`

DECLARE `Exemption` IS ONE OF
    `wholly exempt under` HAS `paragraph` IS AN `Exemption paragraph`
    `partially exempt under` HAS `paragraph` IS AN `Exemption paragraph`
                                 `percentage reduction in taxable value` IS A NUMBER
    `no exemption on these grounds`

GIVEN `the exemption` IS AN `Exemption`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage reduction in taxable value under` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exemption`
    WHEN `wholly exempt under` `p` THEN 100
    WHEN `partially exempt under` `p` `reduction` THEN `reduction`
    WHEN `no exemption on these grounds` THEN 0

-- s 5(12): "The scale for partial exemption from land tax under subsection (10)(b) or (bb) is as follows:"
--   Area used for business or commercial purpose, as % of the total floor area | % reduction in taxable value
--   More than 75%                    Nil
--   75%                              25%
--   70% or more but less than 75%    30%
--   65% or more but less than 70%    35%
--   60% or more but less than 65%    40%
--   55% or more but less than 60%    45%
--   50% or more but less than 55%    50%
--   45% or more but less than 50%    55%
--   40% or more but less than 45%    60%
--   35% or more but less than 40%    65%
--   30% or more but less than 35%    70%
--   25% or more but less than 30%    75%
--   (less than 25%)                  (100%)
DECLARE `Partial exemption band` HAS
    `business area at least, percent` IS A NUMBER
    `reduction in taxable value, percent` IS A NUMBER

-- Highest band first: the first band whose floor the business area reaches is the one that applies.
`the s 5(12) scale` MEANS
    LIST `Partial exemption band` OF 75, 25
         `Partial exemption band` OF 70, 30
         `Partial exemption band` OF 65, 35
         `Partial exemption band` OF 60, 40
         `Partial exemption band` OF 55, 45
         `Partial exemption band` OF 50, 50
         `Partial exemption band` OF 45, 55
         `Partial exemption band` OF 40, 60
         `Partial exemption band` OF 35, 65
         `Partial exemption band` OF 30, 70
         `Partial exemption band` OF 25, 75

GIVEN `bands` IS A LIST OF `Partial exemption band`
      `the business area, percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction from the bands` MEANS
    CONSIDER `bands`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 100
    WHEN `band` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the business area, percent` AT LEAST `band`'s `business area at least, percent`
        THEN `band`'s `reduction in taxable value, percent`
        ELSE `the reduction from the bands` `rest` `the business area, percent`

GIVEN `the business area, percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` MEANS
    IF `the business area, percent` GREATER THAN 75
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the reduction from the bands` `the s 5(12) scale` `the business area, percent`

-- s 5(10)(a): "land may be wholly exempted from land tax if -- (i) the land is owned by a natural person and constitutes
-- his or her principal place of residence (whether or not he or she is the sole owner of the land); and (ii) the
-- buildings on the land have a predominantly residential character; and (iii) no part of the land is used for a business
-- or commercial purpose (other than the business of primary production) or the part of the land so used is less than 25%
-- of the total floor area of all buildings on the land".
-- (b): partially exempted "by reducing its taxable value in accordance with the scale prescribed in subsection (12) if --
-- (i) [as (a)(i)]; and (ii) [as (a)(ii)]; and (iii) a part of the land of 25% or more but not more than 75% of the total
-- floor area of all buildings on the land is used for a business or commercial purpose".
-- (ba): wholly exempted "if -- (i) [as (a)(i)]; and (ii) the buildings on the land are used for the purposes of a hotel,
-- motel, set of serviced holiday apartments or other similar accommodation; and (iii) more than 75% of the total floor
-- area of all buildings on the land is used for the person's principal place of residence".
-- (bb): partially exempted by the s 5(12) scale "if -- (i) [as (a)(i)]; and (ii) [as (ba)(ii)]; and (iii) 25% or more of
-- the total floor area of all buildings on the land is used for the person's principal place of residence, (and for the
-- purposes of the scale prescribed in subsection (12), the area used for the hotel, motel, set of serviced holiday
-- apartments or other similar accommodation will be taken to be the area used for business or commercial purposes)".
-- "principal place of residence" is not defined: a FACT. "natural person" is the Act's term (an individual).
-- One case is one piece of land, at midnight on 30 June before the year (s 4(3)).
DECLARE `Home at midnight on 30 June` HAS
    `it is the principal place of residence of a natural person who owns it`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buildings have a predominantly residential character`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buildings are used for a hotel, motel, serviced holiday apartments or similar accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`                 IS A NUMBER
    `percentage of the total floor area used as the principal place of residence`                  IS A NUMBER

-- `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose` leaves out the business of primary
-- production ((a)(iii)); for a hotel, motel or serviced apartments it is the area used for that accommodation ((bb)).
GIVEN `h` IS A `Home at midnight on 30 June`
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the residential land exemption for the home` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`h`'s `it is the principal place of residence of a natural person who owns it`))
    THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
    ELSE IF `h`'s `the buildings are used for a hotel, motel, serviced holiday apartments or similar accommodation`
         THEN IF `h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used as the principal place of residence` GREATER THAN 75
              THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ba)`
              ELSE IF `h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used as the principal place of residence` AT LEAST 25
                   THEN `partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(bb)`
                            (`the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for`
                                (`h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`))
                   ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`h`'s `the buildings have a predominantly residential character`))
              THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
              ELSE IF `h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose` LESS THAN 25
                   THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`
                   ELSE IF `h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose` AT MOST 75
                        THEN `partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(b)`
                                 (`the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for`
                                     (`h`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`))
                        ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`

§§ `s 5AA -- a minor interest may be disregarded`

-- s 5AA(1): "prescribed land means land that -- (a) is owned by a natural person (the resident) whose interest in the land
-- is not greater than 50% and is also owned by 1 or more other persons; and (b) would, if it were owned solely by the
-- resident, fall within 1 of the grounds for exempting the land from land tax specified in section 5(10)(a) to (bb)".
-- (2): "If the resident's interest in prescribed land is 5% or less, subsection (6) will apply ... unless the
-- Commissioner, on the application of a person who, as an owner of the prescribed land, has an interest exceeding 5% in
-- the land, is satisfied that there is no doubt that the resident's interest was created solely for a purpose, or
-- entirely for purposes, unrelated to reducing the amount of land tax payable". (3): "If the resident's interest in
-- prescribed land exceeds 5% but is less than 50%, subsection (6) will apply ... if the Commissioner forms the opinion
-- that the purpose, or 1 of the purposes, for the creation of the resident's interest was to reduce the amount of land
-- tax payable". (6): the resident "is taken not to be -- (a) an owner of land for the purposes of section 5(10)(a) to
-- (bb) (inclusive) to the extent of the prescribed interest". The Commissioner's satisfaction and opinion are FACTS: the
-- answer is conditional on them.
-- FINDING: an interest of exactly 50% is "not greater than 50%" (prescribed land) but neither "5% or less" nor "less than
-- 50%", so neither (2) nor (3) reaches it.
GIVEN `the resident's interest in the land, percent` IS A NUMBER
      `the land is also owned by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the interest was created solely for purposes unrelated to reducing land tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has formed the opinion that a purpose of creating the interest was to reduce land tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` IF
    IF     (NOT (`the land is also owned by another person`))
        OR `the resident's interest in the land, percent` GREATER THAN 50
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `the resident's interest in the land, percent` AT MOST 5
         THEN NOT (`the Commissioner is satisfied the interest was created solely for purposes unrelated to reducing land tax`)
         ELSE IF `the resident's interest in the land, percent` LESS THAN 50
              THEN `the Commissioner has formed the opinion that a purpose of creating the interest was to reduce land tax`
              ELSE FALSE

-- With s 5AA(6) applied: a resident whose interest is disregarded is not an owner for s 5(10)(a) to (bb), so those
-- grounds fail through that resident. READING: the whole interest is the prescribed interest, so nothing of the
-- exemption through that resident is left; another owner who lives there is a separate case.
GIVEN `h` IS A `Home at midnight on 30 June`
      `the resident's interest is disregarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the residential land exemption after s 5AA` MEANS
    IF `the resident's interest is disregarded`
    THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
    ELSE `the residential land exemption for the home` `h`

§§ `s 5(10)(ab), (ac), (ad), (10a), (10b), (11a) -- a home destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or being built`

-- (ab): wholly exempt if "(i) the land is owned by a natural person (whether or not he or she is the sole owner of the
-- land); and (ii) any buildings on the land of a predominantly residential character are uninhabitable; and (iii) the
-- Commissioner is satisfied -- (A) that the person has ceased to occupy any building on the land of a predominantly
-- residential character because it has been destroyed or rendered uninhabitable by an occurrence for which the person is
-- not responsible (whether directly or indirectly) or which resulted from an accident; and (B) that any such building
-- constituted the person's principal place of residence immediately before ...; and (C) that the person intends to
-- repair or rebuild the building within a period of 3 years from the date on which the building was destroyed or rendered
-- uninhabitable; and (D) that the buildings on the land will, after the completion of building work, have a
-- predominantly residential character; and (E) that the person intends to occupy the land as his or her principal place
-- of residence after the completion of the building work; and (iv) the person is not receiving an exemption from land tax
-- under another provision of this subsection in relation to other land that constitutes the person's principal place of
-- residence". (11a): "land may not be exempted ... under subsection (10)(ab) for a period that exceeds 3 years".
-- (ac): wholly exempt if "(i) the land is owned by a natural person ... who has ceased to occupy the land; and (ii) the
-- buildings on the land immediately before the person ceased to occupy the land had a predominantly residential
-- character; and (iii) [business less than 25% of floor area, as (a)(iii)]; and (iv) the Commissioner is satisfied -- (A)
-- that the person has ceased to occupy the land as his or her principal place of residence because a building on the
-- land is being renovated or rebuilt; and (B) that the buildings ... will, after the completion of the renovation or
-- rebuilding, have a predominantly residential character; and (C) that the person intends to resume occupation of the
-- land as his or her principal place of residence when the renovation or rebuilding work is complete (or is completed to
-- a suitable stage); and (v) [as (ab)(iv)]".
-- (ad): wholly exempt if "(i) the land is owned by a natural person ...; and (ii) [business less than 25%]; and (iii) the
-- Commissioner is satisfied -- (A) that the person is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building or buildings on
-- the land; and (B) [residential after]; and (C) that the person intends to occupy the land as his or her principal place
-- of residence when the renovation or construction work is completed (or is completed to a suitable stage); and (iv) [as
-- (ab)(iv)]".
-- (10a): "Land is not exempt from land tax during a financial year under subsection (10)(ac) or (ad) unless -- (a) the
-- Commissioner is satisfied that -- (i) the owner who applied for the exemption occupies the property as his or her
-- principal place of residence for a period of at least 12 months after completion (or completion to a suitable stage) of
-- the renovation, rebuilding or construction work ...; or (ii) the owner ... intended to so occupy the property when
-- applying for the exemption but there were good reasons why the owner was unable to do so; and (b) the Commissioner is
-- satisfied that no rent or other consideration is paid or payable for occupation by some other person, during the
-- financial year or, in a case where paragraph (a)(i) applies, during the period referred to in paragraph (a)(i)."
-- (10b): "Land may not be exempted ... under subsection (10)(ac) or (ad) for a period that exceeds 2 years unless there
-- are, in the Commissioner's opinion, good reasons to exempt the land for a longer period."
-- Every "the Commissioner is satisfied" is a FACT the owner states: the answer is "exempt, if the Commissioner is so
-- satisfied". READING: the year asked about counts towards the 2-year and 3-year limits, so the land may be exempted
-- for it only if fewer than 2 (or 3) years have already been exempted under the same paragraph.
DECLARE `Kind of building work` IS ONE OF
    `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident`
    `the owner moved out because a building on the land is being renovated or rebuilt`
    `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land`

DECLARE `Building work facts` HAS
    `owned by a natural person`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work`                                                                           IS A `Kind of building work`
    `it was the owner's principal place of residence immediately before`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buildings were predominantly residential before`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buildings will be predominantly residential after the work`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner intends to live there as principal place of residence after the work`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner intends to repair or rebuild within 3 years of the destruction`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`       IS A NUMBER
    `the owner has a residential exemption for other land that is the owner's principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years the land has already been exempted under this paragraph`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner sees good reasons to exempt for longer than 2 years`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `months the owner lives there as principal place of residence after completion`      IS A NUMBER
    `there were good reasons the owner could not live there for 12 months`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `rent or other consideration is paid for someone else's occupation`                  IS A BOOLEAN

`the months the owner must live there after completion` MEANS 12

`the most years under s 5(10)(ab)` MEANS 3

`the most years under s 5(10)(ac) or (ad) without good reasons` MEANS 2

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5(10a) occupation and rent conditions are met` IF
        (    `w`'s `months the owner lives there as principal place of residence after completion` AT LEAST `the months the owner must live there after completion`
         OR  `w`'s `there were good reasons the owner could not live there for 12 months`)
    AND (NOT (`w`'s `rent or other consideration is paid for someone else's occupation`))

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5(10b) 2-year limit is not exceeded` IF
        `w`'s `years the land has already been exempted under this paragraph` LESS THAN `the most years under s 5(10)(ac) or (ad) without good reasons`
    OR  `w`'s `the Commissioner sees good reasons to exempt for longer than 2 years`

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5(10)(ab) grounds exist` IF
        `w`'s `owned by a natural person`
    AND `w`'s `it was the owner's principal place of residence immediately before`
    AND `w`'s `the owner intends to repair or rebuild within 3 years of the destruction`
    AND `w`'s `the buildings will be predominantly residential after the work`
    AND `w`'s `the owner intends to live there as principal place of residence after the work`
    AND (NOT (`w`'s `the owner has a residential exemption for other land that is the owner's principal place of residence`))
    AND `w`'s `years the land has already been exempted under this paragraph` LESS THAN `the most years under s 5(10)(ab)`

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5(10)(ac) grounds exist` IF
        `w`'s `owned by a natural person`
    AND `w`'s `it was the owner's principal place of residence immediately before`
    AND `w`'s `the buildings were predominantly residential before`
    AND `w`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose` LESS THAN 25
    AND `w`'s `the buildings will be predominantly residential after the work`
    AND `w`'s `the owner intends to live there as principal place of residence after the work`
    AND (NOT (`w`'s `the owner has a residential exemption for other land that is the owner's principal place of residence`))
    AND `the s 5(10a) occupation and rent conditions are met` `w`
    AND `the s 5(10b) 2-year limit is not exceeded` `w`

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5(10)(ad) grounds exist` IF
        `w`'s `owned by a natural person`
    AND `w`'s `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose` LESS THAN 25
    AND `w`'s `the buildings will be predominantly residential after the work`
    AND `w`'s `the owner intends to live there as principal place of residence after the work`
    AND (NOT (`w`'s `the owner has a residential exemption for other land that is the owner's principal place of residence`))
    AND `the s 5(10a) occupation and rent conditions are met` `w`
    AND `the s 5(10b) 2-year limit is not exceeded` `w`

GIVEN `w` IS A `Building work facts`
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` MEANS
    CONSIDER `w`'s `the work`
    WHEN `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident` THEN
        IF `the s 5(10)(ab) grounds exist` `w` THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ab)` ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`
    WHEN `the owner moved out because a building on the land is being renovated or rebuilt` THEN
        IF `the s 5(10)(ac) grounds exist` `w` THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ac)` ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`
    WHEN `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` THEN
        IF `the s 5(10)(ad) grounds exist` `w` THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)` ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`

-- (10c): the Commissioner "may, on application under this subsection, grant a waiver or refund of land tax paid or payable
-- ... for a financial year if -- (a) proper grounds for exempting the land from land tax under subsection (10)(ac) or
-- (ad) existed for that financial year; and (b) the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment of the
-- liability to the tax to which the application relates." The same 5 years runs in s 5(12a)(e) and s 5A(4)(c).
`the years after the assessment within which an application may be made` MEANS 5

GIVEN `the date of the assessment` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the date of the application` AT MOST
        DATE_SERIAL (`years after` `the years after the assessment within which an application may be made` `the date of the assessment`)

§§ `s 5(10)(e), (f), (h), (12a) -- retirement villages, relocatable home parks, special disability trusts`

-- (e): "land within a retirement village may be exempted from land tax if -- (i) the land constitutes a residential unit --
-- (A) occupied, under a residence contract, by a natural person as his or her principal place of residence; or (B)
-- available for occupation, under a residence contract, by a natural person as his or her principal place of residence
-- and likely to be so occupied at some time during the ensuing 12 months; or (ii) the land is appurtenant to such a
-- residential unit; or (iii) the land is a facility provided under the retirement village scheme for the exclusive use of
-- residents (and their guests)". "retirement village" and "residence contract" are borrowed from the Retirement Villages
-- Act 1987: FACTS. READING: (e) and (f) say "may be exempted", not "wholly" or "partially"; the land they describe is
-- taken to be wholly exempted.
DECLARE `Retirement village land` IS ONE OF
    `a residential unit occupied under a residence contract by a natural person as principal place of residence`
    `a residential unit available under a residence contract and likely to be so occupied within the next 12 months`
    `land appurtenant to such a residential unit`
    `a facility under the retirement village scheme for the exclusive use of residents and their guests`
    `other land in the village`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Retirement village land`
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the retirement village exemption for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `other land in the village` THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
    OTHERWISE `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(e)`

-- (f): "land within a retired persons' relocatable home park may be exempted from land tax if -- (i) the land constitutes
-- the site for a relocatable home and -- (A) there is a relocatable home on the site owned by a natural person and
-- occupied by the natural person as his or her principal place of residence; or (B) it is likely that within the ensuing
-- 12 months there will be [such a home]; or (ii) the land is appurtenant to such a site; or (iii) the land is a facility
-- provided by the owner of the land for the exclusive use of residents (and their guests)". s 5(13): "retired persons'
-- relocatable home park means land comprising home sites -- (a) that are used (or to be used) for the purpose of
-- establishing 2 or more relocatable homes; and (b) over which rights of occupation for that purpose are granted, by lease
-- or licence, predominantly to persons who are over the age of 55 years and have retired from full-time employment";
-- "relocatable home means a residence that is capable of being moved (in 1 or more sections) from site to site but does
-- not include a caravan, motor home or other moveable structure that can be registered under the Motor Vehicles Act 1959".
DECLARE `Relocatable home park land` IS ONE OF
    `a site with a relocatable home owned and occupied by a natural person as principal place of residence`
    `a site likely to have such a home within the next 12 months`
    `land appurtenant to such a site`
    `a facility provided by the owner for the exclusive use of residents and their guests`
    `other land in the park`

GIVEN `the park has 2 or more home sites for relocatable homes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rights to occupy the sites are granted predominantly to retired people over 55` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a retired persons' relocatable home park` IF
        `the park has 2 or more home sites for relocatable homes`
    AND `rights to occupy the sites are granted predominantly to retired people over 55`

GIVEN `it is such a park` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land` IS A `Relocatable home park land`
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the relocatable home park exemption for` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is such a park`)
    THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the land`
         WHEN `other land in the park` THEN `no exemption on these grounds`
         OTHERWISE `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(f)`

-- (h): wholly exempt if "(i) the land is owned by the trustee of a special disability trust; and (ii) the Commissioner is
-- satisfied that the land constitutes the principal place of residence of the principal beneficiary of the special
-- disability trust." s 5(13): "special disability trust" has its meaning in s 1209L of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)
-- or s 52ZZZW of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (Cth): a FACT.
GIVEN `the land is owned by the trustee of a special disability trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the principal place of residence of the trust's principal beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Exemption`
`the special disability trust exemption` MEANS
    IF `the land is owned by the trustee of a special disability trust` AND `it is the principal place of residence of the trust's principal beneficiary`
    THEN `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(h)`
    ELSE `no exemption on these grounds`

-- (12a): a waiver or refund for a trustee of a special disability trust for a financial year if "(c) the land was acquired
-- by the trustee during the course of the financial year; (d) the Commissioner is satisfied that the land constitutes or
-- will constitute the principal place of residence of the principal beneficiary ... during the course of the financial
-- year; (e) the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment".
GIVEN `the trustee acquired the land during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is or will be the principal beneficiary's principal place of residence during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the assessment` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 5(12a) waiver or refund is open to the trustee` IF
        `the trustee acquired the land during the financial year`
    AND `it is or will be the principal beneficiary's principal place of residence during the year`
    AND `the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment` `the date of the assessment` `the date of the application`

§§ `s 5(4), (6)-(9) -- the exemption notice, and the owner's duties to tell the Commissioner`

-- s 5(6): on exempting land the Commissioner "must ... give notice to an owner of the land -- (a) stating the day ... as
-- from which the exemption is to be effective; and (b) stating the extent of the exemption; and (c) setting out the
-- grounds on which the exemption is granted."
-- s 5(7): "If the factual basis of an exemption as stated in a notice under subsection (6) is wrong or inaccurate, the
-- owner to whom the notice is given must, within 21 days after receipt of the notice, notify the Commissioner of the error
-- or inaccuracy. Maximum penalty: $5 000. Expiation fee: $315." Clock: days from receipt of the notice.
`the days to notify an error in the exemption notice` MEANS 21

`the maximum penalty under s 5(7) or s 5(9)` MEANS 5000

`the expiation fee under s 5(7) or s 5(9)` MEANS 315

GIVEN `the factual basis stated in the notice is wrong or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`s 5(7) -- notify the Commissioner of an error in the exemption notice within 21 days` MEANS
    IF `the factual basis stated in the notice is wrong or inaccurate`
    THEN PARTY `the owner given the exemption notice`
         MUST  `notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy in the exemption notice`
         WITHIN `the days to notify an error in the exemption notice`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the owner given the exemption notice` BECAUSE "s 5(7): the owner must notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy within 21 days after receipt of the notice; maximum penalty $5 000, expiation fee $315"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 5(8): if land is exempted and "circumstances change so that -- (i) proper grounds for an exemption cease to exist; or
-- (ii) proper grounds for an exemption continue to exist but a lesser exemption than the one actually given, the owner
-- must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing of that fact and, whether or not the Commissioner is so informed, the
-- land will cease to be exempt from land tax, or the extent of the exemption will be reduced". (9): failing to is an
-- offence, "Maximum penalty: $5 000. Expiation fee: $315." "Forthwith" names no number of days, so this is not written as
-- a WITHIN rule: the answer is whether the duty arises.
GIVEN `the land is exempted wholly or partially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper grounds for the exemption have ceased to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper grounds now support only a lesser exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing under s 5(8)` IF
        `the land is exempted wholly or partially`
    AND (`proper grounds for the exemption have ceased to exist` OR `proper grounds now support only a lesser exemption`)

-- s 5(4) and s 5A(5): a false or misleading statement in an application: "Maximum penalty: $10 000."
`the maximum penalty for a false or misleading statement in an application` MEANS 10000

§§ `s 5A -- waiver or refund for residential land`

-- s 5A(1): the Commissioner "may, on application under this section, grant -- (a) a waiver or refund of land tax paid or
-- payable by the applicant on land for a particular financial year; or (b) a refund of an amount paid by the applicant as
-- a purchaser of land to the vendor of the land as an adjustment of land tax ... (an amount representing land tax), if --
-- (c) the following criteria are satisfied: (i) the land became the applicant's principal place of residence during the
-- course of the financial year; (ii) proper grounds for exempting the land from land tax under section 5 came into
-- existence when the land became the applicant's principal place of residence; (iii) the applicant must have divested
-- himself or herself, before the end of the financial year, of any other land in respect of which the applicant has had
-- the benefit of a relevant concession for the financial year; (iv) unless the Commissioner allows otherwise in a
-- particular case, no rent or other consideration has been paid or is payable for occupation, during the financial year,
-- of the land or any other land in respect of which the applicant has had the benefit of a relevant concession for the
-- financial year, while the applicant owned both the land and other such land; (v) the criteria for the time being
-- determined by regulation; or (d) in the case of a waiver or refund under paragraph (a), the following criteria are
-- satisfied: (i) the land ceased to be the applicant's principal place of residence during the course of the previous
-- financial year; (ii) proper grounds for exempting the land from land tax under section 5 existed immediately before the
-- land ceased to be the applicant's principal place of residence; (iii) the applicant must have divested himself or
-- herself of the land before the end of the financial year; (iv) [no rent, as (c)(iv), during the financial year or the
-- previous financial year]; (v) the criteria for the time being determined by regulation."
-- (6a): "A person is not eligible ... if the relevant land becomes the person's principal place of residence for a
-- financial year that immediately follows a period of 3 financial years for which the person has had the benefit of an
-- exemption from land tax under section 5(10)(ab) in respect of the same land."
-- The regulations (Land Tax Regulations 2010) are NOT deposited: whether their criteria are met is asked as a FACT. The
-- grant is the Commissioner's ("may"): the answer is whether the criteria are met.
GIVEN `the land became the applicant's principal place of residence during the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper grounds for a s 5 exemption arose when it became the principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant divested, before the end of the year, all other land with a relevant concession for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rent was paid or payable for occupation of either land while the applicant owned both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner allows otherwise despite the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the criteria determined by regulation are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant had a s 5(10)(ab) exemption on this land for the 3 financial years just before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` IF
        `the land became the applicant's principal place of residence during the financial year`
    AND `proper grounds for a s 5 exemption arose when it became the principal place of residence`
    AND `the applicant divested, before the end of the year, all other land with a relevant concession for the year`
    AND ((NOT `rent was paid or payable for occupation of either land while the applicant owned both`) OR `the Commissioner allows otherwise despite the rent`)
    AND `the criteria determined by regulation are met`
    AND (NOT `the applicant had a s 5(10)(ab) exemption on this land for the 3 financial years just before`)

GIVEN `the land ceased to be the applicant's principal place of residence during the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper grounds for a s 5 exemption existed immediately before it ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant divested the land before the end of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rent was paid or payable for occupation of either land while the applicant owned both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner allows otherwise despite the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the criteria determined by regulation are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 5A(1)(d) criteria for a former home are met` IF
        `the land ceased to be the applicant's principal place of residence during the previous financial year`
    AND `proper grounds for a s 5 exemption existed immediately before it ceased`
    AND `the applicant divested the land before the end of the financial year`
    AND ((NOT `rent was paid or payable for occupation of either land while the applicant owned both`) OR `the Commissioner allows otherwise despite the rent`)
    AND `the criteria determined by regulation are met`

§§ `ss 6, 7 -- minimum tax and taxable value`

-- s 6: "Where the total amount of land tax payable by any taxpayer in respect of any year would, apart from this section,
-- be less than $20, no land tax is payable."
`the minimum land tax` MEANS 20

GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the land tax after the s 6 minimum` MEANS
    IF `the amount` LESS THAN `the minimum land tax` THEN 0 ELSE `the amount`

-- s 7(1): "Subject to this Act, the site value of land is its taxable value." (2): site value as determined under the
-- Valuation of Land Act 1971 "as at midnight on 30 June immediately preceding the commencement of that financial year".
-- (3): a corrected or amended determination "must be used". The site value is the Valuer-General's figure: an INPUT
-- (the corrected one, if corrected). s 5(10)(b), (bb): a partial exemption works "by reducing its taxable value"; land
-- wholly exempt is not taxed (s 4(1)(n)).
GIVEN `the site value` IS A NUMBER
      `the exemption` IS AN `Exemption`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable value of the land` MEANS
    `the site value` TIMES (100 MINUS `the percentage reduction in taxable value under` `the exemption`) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `s 8A and Schedule 1 -- the thresholds and the scale`

-- Schedule 1 Part 1: "LT (TA) means the land tax payable with respect to land with a taxable value equal to Threshold A"
-- (and so for TB, TC, TD).
DECLARE `Thresholds` HAS
    `threshold A` IS A NUMBER
    `threshold B` IS A NUMBER
    `threshold C` IS A NUMBER
    `threshold D` IS A NUMBER

-- The dollars charged "for every $100 or fractional part of $100 over" each threshold.
DECLARE `Scale rates` HAS
    `dollars per 100 over threshold A` IS A NUMBER
    `dollars per 100 over threshold B` IS A NUMBER
    `dollars per 100 over threshold C` IS A NUMBER
    `dollars per 100 over threshold D` IS A NUMBER

-- Schedule 1 Part 2 clause 2 (2020/2021 and 2021/2022): Not exceeding Threshold A, Nil; A to B, $0.50 for every $100 or
-- fractional part of $100 over Threshold A; B to C, LT (TB) plus $1.25 ... over Threshold B; C to D, LT (TC) plus $2.00 ...
-- over Threshold C; exceeding D, LT (TD) plus $2.40 ... over Threshold D.
`the clause 2 rates` MEANS `Scale rates` OF 0.50, 1.25, 2.00, 2.40

-- Schedule 1 Part 2 clause 3 (2022/2023 and each subsequent financial year): the same, with $1.00 between B and C.
`the clause 3 rates` MEANS `Scale rates` OF 0.50, 1.00, 2.00, 2.40

-- s 8A(1): land tax "is calculated in accordance with the table in Schedule 1 Part 2 clause 2 for the 2020/2021 and
-- 2021/2022 financial years and in accordance with the table in Schedule 1 Part 2 clause 3 for the 2022/2023 financial
-- year and for each subsequent financial year." The text is as at 1 July 2023, when liability for 2023/2024 arose
-- (s 4(2)). For 2024/2025 and later a change made after that day cannot be seen here: the rates are then an INPUT (the
-- clause 3 rates unless a change is supplied).
`the first year whose rates may have changed after the deposited text` MEANS 2025

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
GIVETH A `Scale rates`
`the scale rates for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` AT MOST 2022
    THEN `the clause 2 rates`
    ELSE IF `the financial year` LESS THAN `the first year whose rates may have changed after the deposited text`
         THEN `the clause 3 rates`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023`
              WHEN JUST `changed` THEN `changed`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN `the clause 3 rates`

GIVEN `r` IS A `Scale rates`, `t` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LT (TB)` MEANS `r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold A` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`t`'s `threshold B` MINUS `t`'s `threshold A`)

GIVEN `r` IS A `Scale rates`, `t` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LT (TC)` MEANS
    `LT (TB)` `r` `t` PLUS (`r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold B` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`t`'s `threshold C` MINUS `t`'s `threshold B`))

GIVEN `r` IS A `Scale rates`, `t` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LT (TD)` MEANS
    `LT (TC)` `r` `t` PLUS (`r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold C` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`t`'s `threshold D` MINUS `t`'s `threshold C`))

-- The table: "Not exceeding Threshold A | Nil"; "Exceeding Threshold A but not exceeding Threshold B | ..."; and so on. A
-- value equal to a threshold belongs to the lower band.
GIVEN `r` IS A `Scale rates`, `t` IS A `Thresholds`, `the taxable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` MEANS
    IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold A`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold B`
         THEN `r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold A` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the taxable value` MINUS `t`'s `threshold A`)
         ELSE IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold C`
              THEN `LT (TB)` `r` `t` PLUS (`r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold B` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the taxable value` MINUS `t`'s `threshold B`))
              ELSE IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold D`
                   THEN `LT (TC)` `r` `t` PLUS (`r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold C` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the taxable value` MINUS `t`'s `threshold C`))
                   ELSE `LT (TD)` `r` `t` PLUS (`r`'s `dollars per 100 over threshold D` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the taxable value` MINUS `t`'s `threshold D`))

-- The thresholds. s 8A(2): for 2020/2021, "Threshold A | $450 000", "Threshold D | $1 350 000"; B and C are the
-- "unadjusted 2010/2011 amount[s]" of $550 000 and $800 000 "adjusted in accordance with subsection (2a)", whose formula
-- is MISSING. (3): for each later year, A, B and C "will be adjusted ... according to the following formula" -- MISSING.
-- (3a): Threshold D is "$1 350 000" for 2021/2022, "$2 000 000" for 2022/2023, and "$2 000 000 adjusted in accordance with
-- subsection (3b)" -- MISSING -- for 2023/2024 and each later year. (7): the Commissioner "must ... by notice in the
-- Gazette, publish the thresholds that will apply"; (8): "rounded to the nearest $1 000 (with an amount of $500 rounded
-- up)"; (9): the notice is "conclusive in all respects". So the thresholds for the year are an INPUT, taken from the
-- Gazette notice. Where the text itself states an amount, that amount is used whatever is supplied (finding 6). A year
-- with no thresholds supplied answers `not covered`.
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`threshold A stated by the Act for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` EQUALS 2021 THEN JUST 450000 ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`threshold D stated by the Act for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` EQUALS 2021 THEN JUST 1350000
    ELSE IF `the financial year` EQUALS 2022 THEN JUST 1350000
         ELSE IF `the financial year` EQUALS 2023 THEN JUST 2000000
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `stated` IS A MAYBE NUMBER, `supplied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated or supplied threshold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `stated`
    WHEN JUST `amount` THEN `amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` `supplied`

`the first year with a Schedule 1 scale` MEANS 2021

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Thresholds`
`the thresholds for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` LESS THAN `the first year with a Schedule 1 scale`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the thresholds supplied`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST `t` THEN
             JUST (`Thresholds` WITH
                       `threshold A` IS `the stated or supplied threshold` (`threshold A stated by the Act for` `the financial year`) (`t`'s `threshold A`)
                       `threshold B` IS `rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` (`t`'s `threshold B`)
                       `threshold C` IS `rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` (`t`'s `threshold C`)
                       `threshold D` IS `the stated or supplied threshold` (`threshold D stated by the Act for` `the financial year`) (`t`'s `threshold D`))

GIVEN `t` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thresholds are in ascending order` IF
        `t`'s `threshold A` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold B`
    AND `t`'s `threshold B` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold C`
    AND `t`'s `threshold C` AT MOST `t`'s `threshold D`

-- The land tax on a taxable value for a year, before the s 6 minimum, or why it cannot be worked out.
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the taxable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the land tax on the scale for the year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year` LESS THAN `the first year with a Schedule 1 scale`
    THEN `not covered` `the assessment year is before 2020/2021: Schedule 1 (inserted from 1 July 2020) has no scale for it, and the earlier scales are not in the deposited text`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the thresholds for` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`
         WHEN JUST `t` THEN
             IF (NOT (`the thresholds are in ascending order` `t`))
             THEN `not covered` `the thresholds supplied are not in ascending order (Threshold A, B, C, D)`
             ELSE `the land tax, in dollars, is`
                      (`the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` (`the scale rates for` `the financial year` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023`) `t` `the taxable value`)

-- The same, after the s 6 minimum: what the taxpayer pays on an assessment.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Land tax answer`
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`after the s 6 minimum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` `amount` THEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` (`the land tax after the s 6 minimum` `amount`)
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the taxable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the land tax payable for the year` MEANS
    `after the s 6 minimum` (`the land tax on the scale for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` `the taxable value`)

§§ `s 8B -- aggregation`

-- s 8B(1): "Except as otherwise provided by this Act, land tax is calculated on the basis of the aggregate taxable value of
-- all land owned by the taxpayer." (2): where the land is in more than one assessment, the tax is "apportioned to and
-- chargeable on the land included in the various assessments in the proportions that the taxable value of the land
-- included in each separate assessment bears to the aggregate taxable value of all the land".
DECLARE `Parcel` HAS
    `site value` IS A NUMBER
    `exemption` IS AN `Exemption`

GIVEN `parcels` IS A LIST OF `Parcel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the aggregate taxable value of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `parcels`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `parcel` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        `the taxable value of the land` (`parcel`'s `site value`) (`parcel`'s `exemption`) PLUS `the aggregate taxable value of` `rest`

GIVEN `the land tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxable value in the assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate taxable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the land tax apportioned to the assessment` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate taxable value` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the land tax` TIMES `the taxable value in the assessment` DIVIDED BY `the aggregate taxable value`

-- s 5A(3): "(a) in the case of a waiver or refund of land tax -- the amount of the waiver or refund is the amount by which
-- the assessment of the taxpayer would have been reduced if the land had been exempt from land tax under section 5;
-- (b) in the case of a refund of an amount representing land tax paid by a purchaser of the land, the amount of the refund
-- is -- (i) the actual amount paid to the vendor by the purchaser as an adjustment of land tax; or (ii) a proportion of the
-- land tax that would be payable on the land for the financial year concerned if the taxpayer owned only that land, being
-- the proportion that the number of days from the date of settlement to the end of that financial year bears to 365,
-- whichever is the lesser." READING: "the number of days from the date of settlement to the end of that financial year"
-- counts the days after the settlement day up to and including 30 June (finding 11).
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the aggregate taxable value with the land` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxable value of the land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the s 5A(3)(a) waiver or refund` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land tax payable for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` `the aggregate taxable value with the land`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` `with` THEN
        CONSIDER `the land tax payable for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023`
                     (`the aggregate taxable value with the land` MINUS `the taxable value of the land`)
        WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
        WHEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` `without` THEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` (`with` MINUS `without`)

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the taxable value of the land` IS A NUMBER
      `the adjustment paid to the vendor` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of settlement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the s 5A(3)(b) refund of an amount representing land tax` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land tax payable for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` `the taxable value of the land`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` `alone` THEN
        `the land tax, in dollars, is`
            (`the lesser of` `the adjustment paid to the vendor`
                (`alone` TIMES (`the days from` `the date of settlement` `to` (`the last day of the financial year` `the financial year`)) DIVIDED BY 365))

§§ `s 9 -- more than one owner`

-- s 9(4): "the owners of the land are to be jointly assessed for land tax on the land as if it were owned by a single
-- person, without regard to -- (a) the separate interest of each owner; or (b) any other land owned by any owner (either
-- alone or with someone else)." (Subject to s 9(2): owners in different capacities, see above.)
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the taxable value of the jointly owned land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the land tax on the joint assessment` MEANS
    `the land tax payable for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` `the taxable value of the jointly owned land`

-- s 9(6): "each owner of the land is to be separately assessed for land tax on -- (a) the owner's individual interest in
-- the land (as if the owner were the owner of a part of the land in proportion to that interest); and (b) any other land
-- owned by the owner alone; and (c) the owner's individual interest in any other land." (8): "there is to be deducted from
-- the land tax assessed for an owner under subsection (6) an amount (if any) necessary to avoid double taxation, being
-- the amount determined by the formula:" -- MISSING from the deposit; its terms are "A is the proportion of the owner's
-- individual interest in the land to the total interests in that land" and "B is the total amount of land tax assessed
-- on the land under subsection (4)". The deduction is therefore an INPUT (from the assessment notice); without it the
-- answer is `not covered`. (9): "If a deduction under subsection (8) would result in a negative amount -- (a) zero is to
-- be substituted for that amount; and (b) the amount of the difference between that amount and zero will not be credited
-- to any liability for land tax". READING: the "negative amount" is the owner's tax after the deduction.
GIVEN `the share, percent` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxable value of the jointly owned land` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxable value of the owner's land owned alone` IS A NUMBER
      `the taxable value of the owner's shares of other jointly owned land` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable value on the separate assessment` MEANS
        `the taxable value of the jointly owned land` TIMES `the share, percent` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the taxable value of the owner's land owned alone`
    PLUS `the taxable value of the owner's shares of other jointly owned land`

GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the thresholds supplied` IS A MAYBE `Thresholds`
      `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` IS A MAYBE `Scale rates`
      `the taxable value on the separate assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 9(8) deduction` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land tax answer`
`the land tax on the separate assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land tax on the scale for the year` `the financial year` `the thresholds supplied` `the rates if changed after 1 July 2023` `the taxable value on the separate assessment`
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `the land tax, in dollars, is` `before the deduction` THEN
        CONSIDER `the s 9(8) deduction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the s 9(8) deduction was not supplied: its formula is missing from the deposited text`
        WHEN JUST `deduction` THEN
            `the land tax, in dollars, is`
                (`the land tax after the s 6 minimum` (`the greater of` 0 (`before the deduction` MINUS `deduction`)))

§§ `s 19 -- paying the land tax, and tax defaults from wrong or missing information`

-- s 19(1): "The amount specified in an assessment by the Commissioner as land tax payable in respect of land for a
-- financial year must be paid to the Commissioner within 30 days after service of the assessment on the taxpayer, or, if
-- there is more than one taxpayer liable to pay the tax in respect of the land, on any one of the taxpayers." Clock: days
-- from service of the assessment (on any one of the taxpayers). A payment of less than the amount does not discharge the
-- duty. Unpaid tax is a "tax default" (TAA s 3(1)), with interest (TAA s 25) and penalty tax (TAA s 30).
`the days to pay land tax after service of the assessment` MEANS 30

GIVEN `the land tax specified in the assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`s 19(1) -- pay the land tax within 30 days after service of the assessment` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `pay the land tax specified in the assessment` `paid` PROVIDED `paid` AT LEAST `the land tax specified in the assessment`
    WITHIN `the days to pay land tax after service of the assessment`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "s 19(1): land tax must be paid within 30 days after service of the assessment; unpaid tax is a tax default under the Taxation Administration Act 1996, with interest (s 25) and penalty tax (s 30)"

-- TAA s 91: an objection "does not in the meantime affect the assessment ... and tax may be recovered as if no objection
-- were pending". So the duty to pay and the objection run side by side. Clock: days from service of the assessment.
GIVEN `the land tax specified in the assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of suspension under s 88` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`s 19(1) with TAA s 91 -- pay within 30 days even while objecting` MEANS
        (`s 19(1) -- pay the land tax within 30 days after service of the assessment` `the land tax specified in the assessment`)
    RAND
        (`TAA Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` `the days of suspension under s 88`)

-- s 19(2): if a person "has not been served with such an assessment or has been served with an assessment for an
-- incorrect amount ... on account of -- (iii) gaining an exemption (or partial exemption) from land tax that should not
-- have applied under this Act (including by an exemption continuing after it should have come to an end); or (iv)
-- receiving a waiver or refund that should not have been given; ... and (b) the failure ... is attributable (wholly or in
-- part) to -- (i) false, misleading or incomplete information that has been provided to the Commissioner; or (ii)
-- information or a notification that should have been provided to the Commissioner not being so provided, then the
-- provision, or non-provision, of that information ... will be taken to constitute a tax default by the person for the
-- purposes of the Taxation Administration Act 1996." (3)(a)(i): the default is taken to have occurred "on the day on
-- which the exemption applied from or the waiver or refund was given"; (c): interest accrues from that day. Paragraphs
-- (v)-(vii) (trusts, s 9(6) interests, related corporations) are out of scope.
GIVEN `no assessment, or one for too little, was served because of an exemption, waiver or refund that should not have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was due to false, misleading or incomplete information, or information or a notification not given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a tax default under s 19(2)` IF
        `no assessment, or one for too little, was served because of an exemption, waiver or refund that should not have applied`
    AND `that was due to false, misleading or incomplete information, or information or a notification not given`
